book></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KUNO YOSHIKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHIMURA TAKUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKECHI HIDEAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMADA MASAZUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>GOTO, SHOICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IITSUKA, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUNO, YOSHIKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIMURA, TAKUYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKECHI, HIDEAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMADA, MASAZUMI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A recording / reproducing apparatus comprising input means for receiving packet data based on the IEEE 1394 and held in a header of a packet based on the IEEE 1394 and containing signal information (hereinafter referred to EMI) on signals representing AV data use license information and recording/reproducing means for recording/reproducing AV data and EMI contained in packet data received by the input means, wherein there are four types of EMI, the recording/reproducing means rewrites the EMI to information of which no more copy is allowed and records the AV data representative of permission that copying one generation is allowed.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un appareil d'enregistrement / reproduction comprenant un dispositif d'entrée pour la réception de paquets de données de type IEEE 1394 et contenu dans une en-tête de paquet IEEE 1394 et contenant des informations de signaux (EMI) se rapportant à des signaux représentant des informations de licence d'utilisation de données audiovisuelles. L'invention porte également sur un appareil d'enregistrement/reproduction destiné à enregistrer/reproduire des données audiovisuelles et des EMI contenues dans un paquet de données reçu par le dispositif d'entrée, à raison de quatre types d'EMI. Le dispositif d'enregistrement/reproduction réécrit les EMI concernant des informations dont on ne peut plus faire de copies, et enregistre les données audiovisuelles d'une autorisation de copier une génération.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>